1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,533
Falling into the Sun

2
00:00:01,533 --> 00:00:02,933
sounds easy. It isn't.

3
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,333
Earth is racing sideways
around the Sun at about

4
00:00:06,333 --> 00:00:07,867
thirty kilometres a second.

5
00:00:07,867 --> 00:00:10,100
And so is everything we
launch from it.

6
00:00:10,733 --> 00:00:13,567
Aim straight at the Sun, and
that sideways speed carries

7
00:00:13,567 --> 00:00:14,467
you right past it.

8
00:00:15,233 --> 00:00:17,867
NASA's Parker Solar Probe
needed to shed about

9
00:00:17,867 --> 00:00:20,300
fifty-three thousand miles
per hour of it.

10
00:00:20,967 --> 00:00:23,267
So it flew past Venus
seven times.

11
00:00:23,267 --> 00:00:26,633
Together, those flybys
reduced its orbital energy

12
00:00:26,633 --> 00:00:29,900
around the Sun, and its
orbit reached closer in.

13
00:00:30,533 --> 00:00:32,467
Then it fell. On
Christmas Eve,

14
00:00:32,467 --> 00:00:35,400
twenty twenty-four, it
passed closer to the Sun

15
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:37,233
than any spacecraft
before it.
